  "description": "CALDEZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C39 H94 Eu4 O13,2(C3 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu7 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu8 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.625-5.659 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 84.44-169.46°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu4(OPrᶦ)10(HOPrᶦ)3]·2HOPrᶦ.",
